+/// Sunshine keeps one source endpoint for the receives of its video and audio
+/// sockets (stream.cpp recvThread). When the first video and audio pings complete
+/// together, the video address can become the audio socket's and no video ever
+/// arrives. The audio stream (and its pings) waits until the host sent video, at
+/// most this long; Sunshine's own ping timeout is 10 s.
+const AUDIO_PING_HOLD: Duration = Duration::from_secs(3);
